#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:5
#: 488fd3e49b3049518611e7450ba31c0a
msgid "CEE-LINE Single-Beam Echosounder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:7
#: 0364809b91b0468db006dd0e2ed9ab50
msgid "The `CEE-LINE single-beam echosounder <https://ceehydrosystems.com/products/single-beam-echo-sounders/cee-line/>`__ can be connected to the autopilot allowing high-resolution, high-reliabiltiy depth data to be obtained live."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:13
#: 42c11438f94f4a92ad9d13181d321472
msgid "Hardware Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:15
#: 0146dc7735854070b5acf3db1f4c56a1
msgid "A standard CEE-LINE kit contains a USB cable.  To work with ardupilot you will need to purchase a CEE-LINE ardupilot cable, available from `CEE HydroSystems <https://ceehydrosystems.com/>`__.  Connect the CEE-LINE ardupilot cable to one of the serial ports (in this example we use Telem2).  The CEE-LINE ardupilot cable is built specifically to connect to telemetry ports and it should not be possible to plug it in incorrectly.  The CEE-LINE will be powered from the Telem2 port, no further connections are required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:17
#: 729f6f3a151f42f7a06c425c69ff671c
msgid "The CEE-LINE is small and can fit into even very small boats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:23
#: 32b092c2a351415ab86da46f93c5eb3f
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:25
#: 93924df9fbf14c05a664e24a3caa8fec
msgid "If the autopilot's Serial2 port (aka Telem2) is used then the following parameters should be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:27
#: ac21c7a72d12402595d8a1fc050b6c2c
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL <SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 9 (Rangefinder)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:28
#: a7164465ba434f5697392bef30a1585f
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_BAUD <SERIAL2_BAUD>` = 9 (9600 baud) to match the default baud rate of the CEE-LINE.  This should be adjusted if the CEE-LINE config changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:30
#: 6c0b680df23e432b974734b2a6babc65
msgid "These rangefinder parameters should also be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:32
#: 4da1e9412c684c6baa9fefef475653a7
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_TYPE <RNGFND1_TYPE>` = 17 (NMEA)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:33
#: 747f3687d41147ff8f16a5295eda9a95
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MIN <RNGFND1_MIN>` = 0.50     - adjust if the CEE-LINE config changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:34
#: 44e089808c634d859fed236be8c1e18c
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_MAX <RNGFND1_MAX>` = 70 (70m) - adjust if the CEE-LINE config changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:35
#: b036f3fe3c42494d82f174895fc493d1
msgid ":ref:`RNGFND1_ORIENT <RNGFND1_ORIENT>` = 25 (down)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:36
#: 3d12d3f20d734a2d987d72484865fb14
msgid ":ref:`FRAME_CLASS` = 2 (boat) - needed if you want the rangefinder reading logged as `DPTH` (and this only works on rover)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:39
#: c8961bc9367f419facd57c8f58dbad5f
msgid "Advanced Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:41
#: df9c6c8a16fe4e12938559eed8af2b6a
msgid "The CEE-LINE is capable of being configured for diverse operating environments.  See the `CEE-LINE documentation <https://ceehydrosystems.com/products/single-beam-echo-sounders/cee-line/>`__ for instructions on adjusting these parameters via a PC connected to the CEE-LINE with the USB cable.  Ardupilot is not capable of adjusting these parameters itself but once they are set, they won't need to be changed and the above configuration works with the CEE-LINE out of the box for plug-and-play simplicity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:44
#: 1b1da2b22d7b48d9a3860f81de358bf9
msgid "Testing the sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:46
#: c47e617cb674426e9f7d3f6ef6ee9c24
msgid "Distances read by the sensor can be seen in the Mission Planner's Flight Data screen's Status tab. Look closely for \"rangefinder1\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:53
#: 4a70cad8c8324344a3209b6e91f7ad2b
msgid "Example Results"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:55
#: 4f4fef14eb384e4687f56cd3ea1c3060
msgid "CEE-LINE data can be extracted directly from the binary logs and plotted using whatever tool you like, for example with `GPS Visualizer <https://www.gpsvisualizer.com/map_input>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ceeline.rst:60
#: 8c9f392a13c94ed58b70ba13c2e40aa1
msgid "The examples here (GPS Visualizer above and Hydromagic below) were created from data collected in a quick 30 minute survey done from the comfort and safety of the shore."
msgstr ""
